Original commit body from ccc895565f4dbbc8dd9e2f947029b680a117cb07:

With --no-default-overlays, _resolve_io_overlay_origins drops every overlay
declaring provenance: community before the load -- including one named by
--io-primitives or a claims file's extra_catalogs -- and stderr says so. But
cmd_verify_claims built catalog_provenance's io_primitives layers from the
RAW flag and claims-file lists, so the report named a file the run never
read as USER-SUPPLIED input with a WITHHELD grant, and the JSON said
user_supplied: true while tiers.yours and tiers.community were empty.

The layers are now derived from the loaded origins (each path tagged with
its layer), and the omitted files -- with their origin -- are passed on and
reported under catalog_provenance.omitted_community_overlays plus a text
NOTE. _resolve_io_overlay_layers / _split_community_overlays return both
halves; _resolve_io_overlay_origins and _omit_community_overlays keep their
shape. The new key is additive inside catalog_provenance, which per the
recorded convention does not bump the envelope version. No verdict changes.

The taint layers (--taint-sources/sinks/sanitizers, extra_catalogs taint
paths) are not filtered by --no-default-overlays, so their disclosure
describes files that were loaded; no mismatch there.

